rivalcfg-gui (1.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 1.6.0.
  * Package the application as a real Python package (rivalcfg_gui/), with
    assets/ and locales/ inside it.  The hand-written per-module install list
    was missing lighting_fx.py and aerox5_mesh.py, both imported by the app, so
    the installed GUI could not start at all.
  * Launch via `python3 -m rivalcfg_gui` from a /usr/bin/rivalcfg-gui wrapper.
    The modules use package-relative imports now and cannot be run as a bare
    script path, which is what the old symlink to rivalcfg_gui.py relied on.
  * Drop debian/install.  dh_install resolves its source paths against the
    source tree root (falling back to debian/tmp); the rules file stages the
    package directory directly into debian/rivalcfg-gui, so those paths could
    never match and dh_install would fail on them.

 -- MrGodzilla38 <oyunustasigodzilla@gmail.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

rivalcfg-gui (1.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 1.4.0.
  * Fix Debian packaging: bundle standalone rivalcfg binary instead of
    depending on unavailable python3-rivalcfg package.
  * Add wget build-dependency for downloading standalone rivalcfg.
  * Change Architecture from 'all' to 'amd64' (bundled binary is x86_64).
  * Add SCRIPT_DIR / _find_rivalcfg() logic: the GUI now prefers a
    bundled rivalcfg binary in its own directory, falling back to PATH.

 -- MrGodzilla38 <oyunustasigodzilla@gmail.com>  Sat, 20 Jun 2026 08:17:24 +0000

